WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.290
Crocomom!

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:06.939
The theory that should not be anything else
but a bunch of people trolling one piece fans.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:15.480
I mean, come on: Crocodile used the be a woman
that had a kid with dragon, and that kid is

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:20.230
Luffy, the protagonist that got impaled by
said crocodile?

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:22.780
Hahaha-yeah no this is totally a thing.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.640
What’s up, I’m Manu, and In case you aren't
familiar with it yet, here's the pitch you

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.800
will usually hear from people who support
this theory.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.460
The idea that Crocodile might be female basically
emerged with the release of the chapter back

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:43.030
in 2009, while the idea that he might be luffy's
mother seems to be from sometime in 2011,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:50.190
although the original post, that is reference
a lot, does not exist anymore.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.310
Basically the idea is based on a single interaction
during the Impel down arc.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:59.600
A single line of dialogue between Ivankov,
one of the leading members of the revolutionary

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.740
army, and Sir Crocodile, the former warlord
that terrorized Alabasta and who was ultimately

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.530
taken down by Luffy.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:13.250
In this scene here, Ivankov basically blackmails
crocodile into helping them, by threatening

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:19.320
to reveal his weakness, a secret debt that
crocodile owes to Ivankov for something he

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:30.140
was given, as Oda confirms later on crocodiles
Vivre Card.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.240
And since Ivankov's most unique power has
been specifically shown to be changing peoples

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:42.119
body's as far as switching genders, the theory
is that Crocodile used to be a woman, Luffy's

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:46.260
mom to be precise, that then was turned into
a man by Ivankov.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:53.869
And, boy, did I have a very emotional roller
coaster-like person journey with this theory.

00:01:53.869 --> 00:01:59.630
Basically ever since this theory was first
brought to my attention years ago, it hasn't

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.840
gone away ever since, ever!

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.880
And so I pracitally went through all 5 stages
of grieve here: First denial.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:13.239
When I first heard about this idea, my reaction
was basically: Haha, this isn't real.

00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:15.599
Someone definitley is trolling these poor
people.

00:02:15.599 --> 00:02:16.989
Then, anger.

00:02:16.989 --> 00:02:22.730
Once I realized that people were taking this
serious and debating if it was possible or

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:28.980
not, I was genuinely pissed people were debating
this seriously, when there were so many other

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.319
great things to talk about with one piece.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:38.050
For example a 30 minute ecstatic rambling
session about where the one piece is... *clears

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:39.050
throat*.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.050
Stage 3: Bargaining.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.609
This is when I started to try and debate people
who believed in this theory and tried to explain

00:02:44.609 --> 00:02:48.620
to people why it was a stupid idea and why
they were wrong.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:49.620
So, so wrong...

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:55.129
I guess I don't have to tell you that those
attempts mostly failed.

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.800
So I entered stage four: Depression.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.189
That was actually quite recently.

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:04.310
I didn't want to talk about Crocomom anymore.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:10.000
I thought there were so many much more interesting
ideas out there that deserved more attention.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:13.489
And so I tried to push the idea out of my
head.

00:03:13.489 --> 00:03:18.840
However everything changed a couple of weeks
ago, when I started working on my most recent

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.390
video on Luffy's mom.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:26.849
I had found out that mothers, or to be precise
their complete and utter absence from one

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:31.390
piece, plays an incredibly central role to
the story.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.779
And of course, I also wanted to discuss a
couple of ideas for who Luffy's mom could

00:03:35.779 --> 00:03:37.230
possibly be.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:43.169
Do you know that feeling when you turn around
and suddenly someone is just standing there?

00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:48.529
That was EXACTLY what it felt like when the
crocomom theory jumped right at me once I

00:03:48.529 --> 00:03:55.979
started to work on this, laughing in my face.

00:03:55.979 --> 00:03:58.219
I had enough of this.

00:03:58.219 --> 00:03:59.370
No more hiding.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:03.639
It was time to switch gears and go into the
offensive.

00:04:03.639 --> 00:04:09.719
I decided to take this stupid theory, dismantle
it to its core and prove to the world once

00:04:09.719 --> 00:04:16.530
and for all that there was no way, NO WAY,
that Crocodile is Luffy's mom.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:23.260
And after sleepless nights of vigorous work,
I finally managed to find the answer to this

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.590
mystery that had tormented me for months.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:30.000
*Sucks in air*, Yeeeah...Crocodile is Luffy's
mom.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.000
*Rubs face*

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.730
So it looks like I've ended up in stage 5.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:34.730
Acceptance.

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:39.630
But, allow me to guide you through my thought
process here and what I found.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:44.940
Because as it turns out there is a lot more
evidence in the story to support this theory

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:47.790
than I originally anticipated.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:54.370
I'm not sure if the person who came up with
this idea had difficulties expressing how

00:04:54.370 --> 00:05:00.810
good it was, or if it was just a super stupid
idea, that turned out to have a lot more depth

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.260
to it by accident.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:08.690
To be honest a lot of the follow-up theories
for crocomom have been pretty damn bad.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:13.760
However I have distilled out the best parts
of everything I could find and added my own

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:16.150
thoughts to this as well.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:21.340
I want to start with the idea that Crocodile
is a woman and then move on to him being luffy's

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.340
mom.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:30.390
Because those are two very different levels
of crazy, that..apparently I'm now part of.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:36.140
Also: *takes breath* please just ignore my
use of pronouns in this video.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:43.090
I'll try my best, but it's probably gonna
be a mess.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:47.170
We've already talked about the most fundamental
thing.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:52.450
With Ivankov, there is actually a power in
One PIece that is able to change genders,

00:05:52.450 --> 00:06:01.490
which is how the entire theory started in
the first place.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:06.120
And the fact that this was shown so closely
to the encounter with Crocodile definitely

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.650
helps the credibility of the two being connected.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:15.440
Plus Ivankov keeps calling him crocoboy in
a what I think is a bit of a mocking way?

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:21.140
Now it could just be, that Ivankov wants to
take away from his manliness, but maybe it's

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:26.500
also supposed to put more attention on exactly
that aspect of his character.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:31.830
Now one thing I think is important to consider
is Oda's inspiration for the warlords.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:36.560
Not only do all of the original Shijibukai
have an animal theme, but the group as a whole

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:44.090
was inspired by the video game Romancing Saga
2, that was released in Japan back in 1993...which

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.270
is older than I am.

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.270
Wow.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:51.819
And each of the warlords shares their characteristics
with one of the heroes of the game.

00:06:51.819 --> 00:06:57.400
For example, there is Rocbouquet-I think is
how you pronounce that - The only female of

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:02.080
the 7, who controls all the men in the Jungle
villages with her charm.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:07.180
Which became Boa Hancock.

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:15.580
Or, Bokuohn - A puppeteer demon who rules
over his own little realm with his own slaves

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:20.940
and who's special technique, "Marionette,"
allows him to manipulate all party members.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:27.320
Which of course is the inspiration for Buggy.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:35.340
*Smirk* The character that is important for
us here is called Wagnas.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:45.400
Who has enslaved an entire country and wants
to find an ancient weapon to control the world.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:55.770
Now, what is really interesting about Wagons
is that while he is male, everything about

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:56.910
him is female.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:03.080
Now, the easiest thing to disprove the idea
that Crocodile is female would be to look

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.280
at his past, clearly showing him to be a guy.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:11.160
And we actually do have two images of crocodile
before the current timeline.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:15.419
One is this sketch Oda made of all the Warlords
as children.

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:19.680
In case you're wondering, Crocodile is here,
a kid who might be either a boy or a girl

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.610
and resembles Hancock most out of all the
others.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.640
The second time is during Roger's execution.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:30.050
However Crocodile is only shown from behind
here.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:36.139
What can be seen is a fur coat, long purple
hair, an earring, and a cigar, both in the

00:08:36.139 --> 00:08:37.819
manga and the anime.

00:08:37.819 --> 00:08:42.569
And since Oda has already done us the favour
and drawn the opposite sex of each of the

00:08:42.569 --> 00:08:49.620
seven, we can say, that this panel of crocodile
from behind would fit with either the male

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:51.889
OR the female version.

00:08:51.889 --> 00:08:56.920
And as you know, Oda sometimes likes to hide
and hint at things in color spreads and cover

00:08:56.920 --> 00:08:57.920
pages.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:05.269
And as it happens, this is the official cover
of chapter 938.

00:09:05.269 --> 00:09:09.259
One thing that I known will stand out to you
by now, because it definitely did to me, is

00:09:09.259 --> 00:09:15.190
that everything surrounding Crocodile is weirdly
connected to gender ideas.

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:20.910
All the codenames of his agents are Mr and
Ms. His name isn't just Desert King Crocodile,

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:24.309
no it's Desert King SIR Crocodile.

00:09:24.309 --> 00:09:26.080
Like Oda going:

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.579
Yeah this man here is very manly by the way.

00:09:29.579 --> 00:09:31.439
No really, he's a sir!

00:09:31.439 --> 00:09:33.390
And a Mr. 0.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:34.390
Croco-BOY.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:40.089
I was considering calling him Sir Testosterone,
that's how manly he is.

00:09:40.089 --> 00:09:46.300
And then there was the introduction of Mr.
2 Bon Clay.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:10:01.459
And the fact 
that this man is part of Crocodile's agency

00:10:01.459 --> 00:10:05.430
is just a pure treasure trove of hints.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:12.389
This man of mans has someone in his strictly
gendered organisation who plays both the male

00:10:12.389 --> 00:10:15.709
AND female part of the double agent theme.

00:10:15.709 --> 00:10:21.620
He is Mr. 2, a number, and also Ms. Bon-Kure,
two festival holidays in Japan.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:26.529
Not only is Bon Clay the first of the discriminated
Okama introduced in the story, that Crocodile

00:10:26.529 --> 00:10:32.660
seems to tolerate and integrate just fine
into his plans, but he also has the ability

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:40.579
to change faces, from man to woman to man,
becoming someone completely different.

00:10:40.579 --> 00:10:50.680
Now if this isn't hinting at something...but
there's even more to this.

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.920
Bon Clay, as one of the Okama, comes from
Okama island.

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:59.170
An Island that not only gives us the connection
between Ivankov and Crocodile, but more importantly

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.459
between Crocodile and Dragon.

00:11:02.459 --> 00:11:09.040
Most of the Okama are part of the Revolutionary
army, who's leader is none other than Dragon,

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:10.240
Luffy's father.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.240
So.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:16.839
All this so far has mostly served as my argument
that Crocodile used to be a woman.

00:11:16.839 --> 00:11:21.329
Which actually has support by large parts
of the fandom.

00:11:21.329 --> 00:11:26.980
However, and I totally understand why, saying
that Crocodile was a woman and that Crocodile

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:32.019
is Luffy's mother are two very VERY different
cups of tea.

00:11:32.019 --> 00:11:35.209
More like a cup of tea and a cup of coffee.

00:11:35.209 --> 00:11:36.209
And STILL!

00:11:36.209 --> 00:11:39.750
I believe that both of these things are true.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:40.750
Here's why.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:44.990
By the way, in case you enjoy theories like
these and want to delve deeper into the endlessly

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:50.360
deep and hopelessly fascinating lore of one
piece with me every single week, I'd love

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.660
for you to consider subscribing to my channel.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:57.249
Now there are a couple of really big arguments
that seem to bury the Crocomom idea fairly

00:11:57.249 --> 00:12:03.680
quickly, which I know well, because I used
to use them quite a lot back in the day.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:09.830
First: If Crocodile was Luffy's mom, why didn't
he recognise him.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:12.949
Well, because he hadn't seen luffy since he
was a baby.

00:12:12.949 --> 00:12:18.759
Okay, but then why didn't crocodile recognise
his last name if he had a kid with Dragon?

00:12:18.759 --> 00:12:24.329
Well for the same reason no-one else knew
that Luffy was related to Dragon or that Garp

00:12:24.329 --> 00:12:25.329
was related to dragon.

00:12:25.329 --> 00:12:39.199
Dragon 
never shared his last name until it was revealed

00:12:39.199 --> 00:12:46.670
during the war.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:49.019
Even Ivankov didn't reckognize Luffy's name.

00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:54.309
Now if Luffy were Crocodile's child, wouldn't
they have some similarities?

00:12:54.309 --> 00:12:56.369
Well, they do.

00:12:56.369 --> 00:13:02.480
Both of them have the undying loyalty of their
crews, with Das Bones still following him

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:06.389
after impel down, the Zoro to Baroque works
luffy.

00:13:06.389 --> 00:13:12.220
In a way, crocodile, just like Moria, had
his dreams crushed at some point by whitebeard,

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:21.670
basically showing us a version of Luffy that
had given up on his dreams.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:28.949
Which is accentuated by how he constantly
lectures luffy during there first two encounters.

00:13:28.949 --> 00:13:34.480
Plus in the mafia special, Luffy literally
looks like Crocodile.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:38.480
And there is also this great comic of Luffy
turning into crocodile.

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.190
Though admittedly that's not canon.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:47.970
So, at least now we know that Crocodile did
not know that Luffy was Dragon's child and

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:53.130
so he has an excuse for impaling and mortally
wounding his potential kid.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:55.509
But that doesn't proof anything yet.

00:13:55.509 --> 00:14:01.589
Nooo, because for that we have to look at
Marineford and specifically Crocodile's actions

00:14:01.589 --> 00:14:06.279
during marineford after it was revealed that
Luffy was dragon's son.

00:14:06.279 --> 00:14:12.439
Because after his initial attempt to attack
Whitebeard, eh actually did a few things that

00:14:12.439 --> 00:14:18.199
seemed extremely out of character, because
he went of his way and endangered himself

00:14:18.199 --> 00:14:21.410
without really needing to.

00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:26.610
And keep in mind that we never got to see
his reaction to the Luffy-Dragon reveal, just

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:30.930
as we got no reaction to rogers execution.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:40.069
Here's all the out of character stuff he suddenly
started doing.

00:14:40.069 --> 00:14:46.009
He stopped Ace's execution with the excuse
that he didn't want Sengoku to have the pleasure

00:14:46.009 --> 00:14:51.730
of victory, which if you ask me is pig pile
of poop.

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:56.600
Some people will tell you it’s because Luffy
inspired him like Luffy does many others,

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:04.249
but what exactly is Luffy doing in Marineford
that he didn’t in Impel Down or even Alabasta?

00:15:04.249 --> 00:15:05.989
Nothing.

00:15:05.989 --> 00:15:11.860
That means Crocodile would have an entire
change of heart for no apparent reason whatsoever,

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:15.079
and completely off screen.

00:15:15.079 --> 00:15:30.019
Then, he and Das bones hold of Mihawk to help
Luffy.

00:15:30.019 --> 00:15:36.059
Suddenly Crocodile orders his only remaining
loyal man to protect the life of the person

00:15:36.059 --> 00:15:40.069
that ruined his plans and put him in prison?

00:15:40.069 --> 00:15:44.839
He might have to refrain from killing Luffy
because of Ivankov, but he surely wouldn't

00:15:44.839 --> 00:15:48.889
go out of his way to send his best man off
for him.

00:15:48.889 --> 00:15:57.069
And When Mihawk questions why he’d protect
Luffy, Crocodile’s only response is this:

00:15:57.069 --> 00:16:02.040
[not in the best mood]

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:06.199
Again, why should he suddenly be in a bad
mood?

00:16:06.199 --> 00:16:12.529
Maybe because he just found out he once stabbed
his own child in the gut and left him to die?!

00:16:12.529 --> 00:16:19.299
But if those weren't enough yet, he does the
unthinkable and faces off with Akainu, probably

00:16:19.299 --> 00:16:29.959
the strongest person present in the entire
war.

00:16:29.959 --> 00:16:35.490
So the fact that as Luffy is laying there
uncouncious and weak, with Jimbe slumped over

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:41.619
him, Akainu about to deliver the final blow,
Crocodile coming out of no where to save him

00:16:41.619 --> 00:16:46.619
and safely transporting him to law, is once
again is so telling.

00:16:46.619 --> 00:16:51.769
This is a man that shouldn't have been on
luffy's side for so many reasons, that has

00:16:51.769 --> 00:16:58.649
left people behind for being useless or too
week, seemingly out of nowhere goes full Zoro-mode

00:16:58.649 --> 00:17:07.730
for Luffy, willing to sacrifice himself for
luffy.

00:17:07.730 --> 00:17:13.010
There were plenty of other characters that
could have essentially done the same exact

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:16.730
thing, but Oda choice to have Crocodile.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:21.110
Who then has this epic shot.

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:27.690
Standing side by side with all of the whitebeard
commanders, his sworn enemies, as a protective

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:34.270
mother that would sacrifice anything for her
child, because Crocodile now knows that Luffy

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.050
is his son.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:40.730
Mothers in one piece play an incredibly important
role and there are also a few other possibilities

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:42.610
for Luffy's mom.

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:51.680
Make sure to check out that video here if
you haven't seen it.

